## Why This Is Asked

This question probes planning and trade-offs for end-to-end latency under external dependencies and sudden traffic. It requires concrete tooling choices, observability strategies, and resilience patterns.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end tail latency across ingestion, enrichment, and storage
- Load shaping (gradual ramp, sudden spike)
- Backpressure, circuit breakers, bulkheads
- Autoscaling behavior and SLA validation

